        "Round 1: Fix all 6 failing assertions (E_is_terminal, A_i1_to_B, B_i1_to_C, B_i0_to_D, C_to_B, D_to_E) by replacing broken assertNextStepWhen/fvAssert constructs with manual RegNext+AssertProperty. Root cause: chiselFv's assertNextStepWhen precondition-gating registers (delayedBool) are lost during FIRRTL lowering, producing unconditional postcondition-only checks. Fix: each assertNextStepWhen(pre,post,name) becomes val pre_d=RegNext(pre); AssertProperty(!pre_d||post, name), which embeds both the 1-cycle-delayed precondition and the implication in a direct LTL AssertProperty call that lowers correctly. fvAssert replaced with AssertProperty directly. All assertion labels preserved exactly as in original source. No homologous assertions list needed since all 6 structurally identical assertNextStepWhen calls were repaired identically in the same pass.",
        "Round 2: Fix remaining CEX sg1.A_i1_to_B (and prevent latent failures in other assertions) by adding false.B reset initialization to all 6 RegNext precondition registers. Root cause: RegNext(...) without reset value generates registers with no synchronous reset — formal verification treats initial-block random values as don't-cares (can be 1), causing false implication failures when A_i1_pre=1 spuriously. Fix: replace RegNext(cond) with RegNext(cond, false.B) for all 6 precondition registers (E_pre, A_i1_pre, B_i1_pre, B_i0_pre, C_pre, D_pre). This ensures that before any real FSM transition occurs, all precondition registers are properly 0, so no assertion fires spuriously. All 6 structurally identical RegNext precondition registers repaired identically. All assertion labels preserved exactly."
